IMDb Top 250 Movie Recommender System

This project builds a recommendation engine that suggests similar movies based on storyline content from IMDb's Top 250 list. It uses web scraping to gather movie titles and plot summaries, then applies natural language processing techniques to compare movie plots using TF-IDF and cosine similarity.

There are two implementations:

- Manual TF-IDF Version: Calculates term frequency and inverse document frequency from scratch, offering full transparency into the vectorization process.

- Scikit-learn TF-IDF Version: Uses TfidfVectorizer for efficient and scalable computation.

How it works:
- Scrape IMDb movie titles and plot summaries using BeautifulSoup
- Normalize and tokenize the text, removing stopwords
- Vectorize movie plots using TF-IDF (manually or via scikit-learn)
- Accept user input as a storyline
- Compute cosine similarity between the input and all movies
- Return the top N most similar titles

Technologies used: Python, requests, BeautifulSoup, concurrent.futures, re, math, scikit-learn

Future enhancements may include genre filtering, GUI integration, or deploying as a web app.
